{"name":"In a Nutshell","hex":"#b98052","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"in a nutshell","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["In summary; briefly or simply."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/in_a_nutshell"}],"entries":[{"title":"Kurzgesagt","blocks":[{"text":"Kurzgesagt is a German animation and design studio founded by Philipp Dettmer. The studio is best known for its YouTube channel, which is well known for its animated educational content using minimalistic, flat and in some cases with 3D graphics. It discusses scientific, technological, political, philosophical, and psychological subjects."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/65/Kurzgesagt.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kurzgesagt"},{"title":"In a Nutshell","blocks":[{"text":"In a Nutshell is a musical composition by Percy Aldridge Grainger for orchestra, piano, and Deagan percussion instruments. The suite, published in 1916, is made up of four movements: \"Arrival Platform Humlet\", \"Gay But Wistful\", \"Pastoral\", and \"The Gum-Suckers March\". Grainger later made versions for both solo piano and piano duo. It is described as one of the early modernist works of Grainger."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/In_a_Nutshell_Suite_Title_Page.png/330px-In_a_Nutshell_Suite_Title_Page.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/In_a_Nutshell"},{"title":"Nutshell","blocks":[{"text":"A nutshell is the outer shell of a nut. Most nutshells are inedible and are removed before eating the nut meat inside. It covers and protects the kernel, which may be edible."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Whole_walnut_kernel_and_shell.jpg/330px-Whole_walnut_kernel_and_shell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","lin